on/math-academy-id "q-140519" :question/problem "Given that $A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -8 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}],$ find the sum of the eigenvalues of $A.$" :question/worked-solution "The characteristic polynomial of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(\\lambda ) & ={\\lambda }^{2}-\\text{tr}(A)\\lambda +\\text{det}(A).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using Vieta's formulas, we have that the roots of $p(\\lambda ),$ i.e. the eigenvalues of $A,$ satisfy\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{1}+{\\lambda }_{2}=\\text{tr}(A) \\\\ {\\lambda }_{1}\\cdot {\\lambda }_{2}=\\text{det}(A).\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the sum of the eigenvalues of $A$ is equal to the trace of $A.$ \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}+{\\lambda }_{2}=\\text{tr}(A)=4+1=5.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-140519/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "87febdb4-5f54-5aff-b84a-1b05359d6b57"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-140519"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-85923/selection/283bc09f1a097ae8400558511ca45f1013e17c797fdb7407be52694190fd744b" :answer/id #uuid "93821c26-2642-5bcb-808c-1f425fb4a72c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85923/selection/0fbe558572ecce67593db00d22f0d8d9d09c98d019451cd13488790a441e6c9c" :answer/id #uuid "1e573334-7326-5217-97eb-42c3cb17cc49" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85923/selection/5d022a88a643e97abec4d01dfce48411101475c0705a98f29f3a8e3560fb0616" :answer/id #uuid "4d7e5e06-483b-5aed-b36b-6143e564f6c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85923/selection/a84d639d380e10cb74c92005685f9f65779377dfb51342c280c63c645679bbea" :answer/id #uuid "0dc2d6b2-00d2-555d-a84d-4ef37d35c5c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85923/selection/e0e0a3ac4fe95f021c8f8aece7092270d36ad30c356733db1e628dc4f0b1d434" :answer/id #uuid "affbceeb-a37b-5175-bcc8-69954b392fc5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85923/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d3d33020-62f2-5332-8ccc-76e65d5a2f5a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-85923/selection/e0e0a3ac4fe95f021c8f8aece7092270d36ad30c356733db1e628dc4f0b1d434" :answer-field/choices ["q-85923/selection/283bc09f1a097ae8400558511ca45f1013e17c797fdb7407be52694190fd744b" "q-85923/selection/0fbe558572ecce67593db00d22f0d8d9d09c98d019451cd13488790a441e6c9c" "q-85923/selection/5d022a88a643e97abec4d01dfce48411101475c0705a98f29f3a8e3560fb0616" "q-85923/selection/a84d639d380e10cb74c92005685f9f65779377dfb51342c280c63c645679bbea" "q-85923/selection/e0e0a3ac4fe95f021c8f8aece7092270d36ad30c356733db1e628dc4f0b1d434"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-85923" :question/id #uuid "91203007-4206-5b75-bc29-6bbb4b83094f" :question/math-academy-id "q-85923" :question/problem "Given that $A=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & -3\\end{aligned}],$ find the product of the eigenvalues of $A.$" :question/worked-solution "The characteristic polynomial of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(\\lambda ) & ={\\lambda }^{2}-\\text{tr}(A)\\lambda +\\text{det}(A).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using Vieta's Formulas, we have that the roots of $p(\\lambda ),$ i.e. the eigenvalues of $A,$ satisfy\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{1}+{\\lambda }_{2}=\\text{tr}(A) \\\\ {\\lambda }_{1}\\cdot {\\lambda }_{2}=\\text{det}(A).\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the product of the eigenvalues of $A$ is equal to the determinant of $A.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{1}\\cdot {\\lambda }_{2} & =det(A) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & 2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =5\\cdot (-3)-\\sqrt{5}\\cdot 2\\sqrt{5} \\\\  & =-15-10 \\\\  & =-25.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-85923/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "87febdb4-5f54-5aff-b84a-1b05359d6b57"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-85923"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-38720"] :question/problem "Given that $A=[\\begin{aligned}-12 & 7 \\\\ 9 & 3\\end{aligned}],$ find the sum of the eigenvalues of $A.$" :question/worked-solution "The characteristic polynomial of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(\\lambda ) & ={\\lambda }^{2}-\\text{tr}(A)\\lambda +\\text{det}(A).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using Vieta's formulas, we have that the roots of $p(\\lambda ),$ i.e. the eigenvalues of $A,$ satisfy\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{1}+{\\lambda }_{2}=\\text{tr}(A) \\\\ {\\lambda }_{1}\\cdot {\\lambda }_{2}=\\text{det}(A).\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the sum of the eigenvalues of $A$ is equal to the trace of $A.$ \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}+{\\lambda }_{2}=\\text{tr}(A)=-12+3=-9.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-85924/selection/aeea0fa93ef38f179f4ffaa74583746c3dadf928a39f66fc07db0c0e0392d1d5" :answer/id #uuid "22e2a937-7d38-5465-98ea-b31e75c3c877" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{A}^{2}-3A+16I" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85924/selection/d19e38c785f23903e324a4391a52c10d4198bcee649724ee3f1bef66ef88768b" :answer/id #uuid "f91faa89-e322-5df0-a019-04f9e97e0935" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{A}^{2}-3A+6I" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85924/selection/a0ddb1795d6541fa49edc8d217e400d16330ee81d7373cdb57b8e4c75bcaf6fa" :answer/id #uuid "a4ac3bcc-c368-5258-9890-e5aed2ceee3c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{A}^{2}+3A-16I" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85924/selection/b7d12e535bcaf79bcc37bae0e037299c09e